From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evan Stade <evanstade@microsoft.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:41:31 -0700
Subject: [M156] Avoid UAFs in BlobStorageContext

Original change's description:
> Avoid UAFs in BlobStorageContext
>
> Many different flows could lead to a UAF of a BlobEntry*. The basic
> story is:
>
> 1. BlobEntry A transitively holds some BlobDataHandle for B
>
> 2. Some operation on A, such as FinishBuilding, drops said handle for B
>
> 3. B has no more handles and stops using memory, freeing up memory for
> some other BlobDataHandle C which had been blocked on quota
>
> 4. error occurs while C is acting on this, C self destructs
>
> 5. turns out C was the only thing holding A alive; A is destroyed
>
> 6. the rest of FinishLoading (or another method) continues, and doesn't
> realize `BlobEntry* a` is now deleted.
>
> A small twist on this story: `ClearAndFreeMemory(entry)` was also
> re-entrant, because it can trigger a self-deletion similar to the above,
> where `ClearAndFreeMemory` is called for the second time in
> `DecrementBlobRefCount`. But `ClearAndFreeMemory` is mostly unnecessary
> when the BlobEntry is already being deleted, so don't call it explicitly
> on `DecrementBlobRefCount`, instead making it effectively part of
> `~BlobEntry`.
>
> Since this is a broad class of issues, it's not easy to spot-fix to
> produce a small change. Instead of pervasively passing around
> `BlobEntry*`, pass around `scoped_refptr<BlobEntry>`, so that it won't
> be deleted out from under other operations.
>
> Confusingly, `BlobDataHandle` is already a sort of ref counting, and
> `BlobEntry` contains symbol names like `ref_count` and such; those are
> renamed to "handle count" instead to avoid confusing with
> `base::RefCounted`.
>
